# Program-lifetime lazy_static caches in the x509-parser dependency chain
# (EXTENSION_PARSERS, OID_REGISTRY, ATTRIBUTE_PARSERS, and any future sibling).
# hashbrown keeps an interior `ctrl` pointer into the middle of its allocation,
# so valgrind cannot see the root held by the static and classifies the block as
# "possibly lost" instead of "still reachable". One entry keyed on lazy_static's
# initializer covers every such static, so a newly-touched one cannot reopen this.
#
# match-leak-kinds is explicit so the entry stays correct even if the
# --show-leak-kinds flag in .github/workflows/memory_leak.yml is ever relaxed.
{
   lazy-static-program-lifetime-caches
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible,reachable
   ...
   fun:*__static_ref_initialize*
}
